course: dictionary
lesson: 15551
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Read the rest of the sentence to find out which one the writer means. «The superstar signed autographs for her fans.» Here a superstar is a famous performer, because the fans and the autographs show that she is well known.
explain: Now read this: «You're a superstar for helping me with my bike!» Nobody thinks you are a famous singer. The writer means you did a brilliant job, so this is informal praise.
explain: Ask yourself: is this person famous, or has someone done something really well? The clues around the word tell you which. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A superstar is an extremely famous and successful singer, actor, sports player or other performer.
fact: Informally, a superstar is someone who is brilliant at something or who has done a great job.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «a pop superstar», «a football superstar» and «become a superstar».
fact: Teachers and parents sometimes say «You're a superstar!» to praise a child for helping.
fact: In media lessons, pupils look at how superstars are shown in magazines and online, and how photos may be edited.
exercise: «The football superstar scored three goals in one game.» What is a superstar here? | A large stadium with rows of seats | A ball used in a match | A teacher who marks football games | *A famous and successful sports player
exercise: «You're a superstar for tidying the classroom!» What does superstar mean here? | A famous actor on television | *Someone who has done a brilliant job | A person who is always late | A star you can see in the night sky
exercise: Which phrase means someone has become very famous? | eat a sandwich | *become a superstar | tidy the desk | ride a bike
test: What kind of superstar is in «The pop superstar sang to thousands of people»? | A tired teacher | *A famous singer | A new school bus | A lost dog
test: Lily says to her friend, «You're a superstar for sharing your pencils!» What does Lily mean? | You are a star in the sky | *You did something kind and helpful | You have lost your pencils | You are famous on television
exam: Which sentence uses superstar to mean someone who did a great job? | The superstar walked the red carpet at the awards. | The superstar's new album sold a million copies. | A superstar is always on the news. | *Mum says, «You're a superstar for cleaning your room!»
